HYME","locations":[1,4,5,8],"groups":["A","B"],"obligations":[],"subject":[]},{"code":"MANDATE_GROUPS_INDISTINGUISHABLE","severity":"note","message":"groups A [1, 4] and C [9, 12] would pass as ONE group — every cross pair scores at or above the collision cut (0.9), rhyme or near rhyme alike (the edges below name which) — so the mandate splits a group the graph does not, and each of the 4 cross pairs is reported as a collision purely because the letters differ","evidence":"derived from the rhyme graph; the mandate cannot state a return (doctrine 2: a letter is a property of a LINE, so no letter scheme can say 'these two groups are the same words coming back'). THIS DOES NOT SAY WHICH IT IS: a section returning and a rhyme sound reused by accident are the same picture in the graph, and the loop does not read intent out of a score. If it is a return, declare it and these stop being findings; if it is not, one of the two groups needs a different sound. Edges: L1~L9 'king-'~'king-' 1.000 ASSONANCE+CONSONANCE+REPEAT+RHYME; L1~L12 'king-'~'wing' 1.000 ASSONANCE+CONSONANCE+RHYME; L4~L9 'wing'~'king-' 1.000 ASSONANCE+CONSONANCE+RHYME; L4~L12 'wing'~'wing' 1.000 ASSONANCE+CONSONANCE+REPEAT+RHYME","locations":[1,4,9,12],"groups":["A","C"],"obligations":[],"subject":[]},{"code":"MANDATE_GROUPS_INDISTINGUISHABLE","severity":"note","message":"groups A [1, 4] and D [13, 16] would pass as ONE group — every cross pair scores at or above the collision cut (0.9), rhyme or near rhyme alike (the edges below name which) — so the mandate splits a group the graph does not, and each of the 4 cross pairs is reported as a collision purely because the letters differ","evidence":"derived from the rhyme graph; the mandate cannot state a return (doctrine 2: a letter is a property of a LINE, so no letter scheme can say 'these two groups are the same words coming back'). THIS DOES NOT SAY WHICH IT IS: a section returning and a rhyme sound reused by accident are the same picture in the graph, and t